activation	Print prompt	2026-10-27T08:45:51.2129550Z {"title": "Wrong result for correlated EXISTS with rowid predicate when optimizer is enabled", "body": "### What happens?\n\nA correlated `EXISTS` query returns an incorrect result when the optimizer is enabled.\n\nWith the default optimizer settings, an `INNER JOIN` using the same predicate returns 1 row, while the corresponding `EXISTS` query returns 0 rows.\n\nAfter disabling the optimizer with `PRAGMA disable_optimizer`, both queries return 1.\n\nThe right-hand table contains exactly one row, so for this test case the `INNER JOIN` and `EXISTS` forms should agree on whether the single left-hand row has a match.\n\nThe incorrect result only occurs with the optimizer enabled.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE t75(c0 INTEGER);\nCREATE TABLE t0(c0 INTEGER);\n\nINSERT INTO t75 VALUES (1);\nINSERT INTO t0 VALUES (0);\n\nSELECT 'INNER_JOIN' AS q, COUNT(*) AS n\nFROM t75 l\nJOIN t0 r\n  ON l.rowid <= r.rowid\n AND l.c0 <> r.c0;\n\nSELECT 'EXISTS' AS q, COUNT(*) AS n\nFROM t75 l\nWHERE EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1\n    FROM t0 r\n    WHERE l.rowid <= r.rowid\n      AND l.c0 <> r.c0\n);\n```\n\nWith the optimizer enabled, I get:\n\n```text\nINNER_JOIN | 1\nEXISTS     | 0\n```\n\nThe expected result is:\n\n```text\nINNER_JOIN | 1\nEXISTS     | 1\n```\n\nDisabling the optimizer makes both queries return the expected result:\n\n```sql\nPRAGMA disable_optimizer;\n\nSELECT 'INNER_JOIN_optimizer_off' AS q, COUNT(*) AS n\nFROM t75 l\nJOIN t0 r\n  ON l.rowid <= r.rowid\n AND l.c0 <> r.c0;\n\nSELECT 'EXISTS_optimizer_off' AS q, COUNT(*) AS n\nFROM t75 l\nWHERE EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1\n    FROM t0 r\n    WHERE l.rowid <= r.rowid\n      AND l.c0 <> r.c0\n);\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```text\nINNER_JOIN_optimizer_off | 1\nEXISTS_optimizer_off     | 1\n```\n\nFor the only rows in the two tables, both `rowid` values are 0, so:\n\n```text\nl.rowid <= r.rowid\n0 <= 0\nTRUE\n```\n\nand:\n\n```text\nl.c0 <> r.c0\n1 <> 0\nTRUE\n```\n\nTherefore the predicate is satisfied.\n\nSince `t0` contains exactly one row, the `EXISTS` predicate should be true for the single row in `t75`, and the result should be 1 rather than 0.\n\n### OS:\n\nUbuntu 2404\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.5\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nJDBC\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nAnn C\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nNanchang University\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nYes"}
